R("the corner stones can be drawn floor by floor, a mock-up for her to choose (?house=alt|tint|here, ?house=off; DV)", "the corner stones are drawn floor by floor in a pastel, the floor's wallpaper colour, nothing else coloured, paper plain (DV; EB, her 13:42 'the doll's house: 3')")
R("all 88 keys and their eight Cs. The dashboard", "all 88 keys and their eight Cs; EB (her 13:42 'concisely') put three of them inside the pads they repeated (the keyboard and the bass in Pluck, push or strike, the playground in The pedals, the slide in Grand, upright, 88 keys), Strum the strings stays a step's own. EB also took out of their steps the toys that repeated the step (My word tune, Loud and soft your way, Drive the tempo, Make a rhythm card, Climb the ladders, My tune my chords; they stay in the toolbox) and drew the grand on longer legs (her 'c'). Rhythm, Grade 2 has Split the beat with its six ways (DZ); MelodyStaff's stems meet their heads (EA). The dashboard")
R("1. Fun spread through every room (her 11:33; the audit in sc/fun41.js: of 314 lesson steps 27 let you make something, 7 are games, 51 only listen-then-quiz): DY, the in-a-row game on every asking activity, once she has seen it; a play-along challenge in each Grade 6 to 8 scales and arpeggios room; a make-it toy for Intervals, Grade 2, Rhythm, Grade 2 and Scales, Grade 3. Her picks waiting: the doll's house corner stones (?house=alt|tint|here, or none) and the grand's legs (b, c or d). Then the rest of call 39, the Workbooks fun first, a Pieces shelf (her 22:31) once she says which grade and what for.",
  "1. Call 41, the Reference (her 14:32 'a space that takes in the whole, like a book's reference pages', 14:36 'all at once'): one table per topic, Beginner to Grade 8, each row a door into the room that teaches it; on screen (the Home's Quick line) and on paper; the Scales map and the dictionary inside it. Then the rest of call 39, the Workbooks fun first, a Pieces shelf (her 22:31) once she says which grade and what for.")
io.open(md, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)
h = io.open(hist, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(h) if l.startswith('| 769 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1 and not any(l.startswith('| 770 |') for l in h)
h[idx[0] + 1:idx[0] + 1] = [
 "| 770 | 2026-10-31 | **Rhythm, Grade 2's thing to make (Build DZ; the fun audit's gap).** Split the beat takes its ways, its stars and its store (BeatSplit kinds, starsDef, sk): Rhythm, Grade 2's has the six ways the room teaches (crotchet, two quavers, four semiquavers, quaver and two semiquavers, two semiquavers and a quaver, the triplet; the dotted ones are Grade 3), in step 2 (Triplets and duplets); Grade 3's keeps seven. A toy for Intervals, Grade 2 was drafted and left out: its own pad already sounds every interval above the tonic. Test sc/dz802.js. |",
 "| 771 | 2026-10-31 | **The last hanging stems (Build EA; her 09:38 'check for any like this').** Call 40 opened the toys in their steps and the stem audit found the older MelodyStaff (Add a sharp or a flat, and 30 more uses) with its stems 6 from the head's centre and a pixel off it: now 5.57 for the filled 6.4 x 4.6 head and 6.93 for the hollow one with its stroke, from the centre, flags and beams with them; the syncopation picture's second and third stems (Rhythm, Grade 4's checks) sit like its first. The audit's six left are bar lines beside a note and two borderline pictograms. |",
 "| 772 | 2026-10-31 | **Concise (Build EB; her 13:42: 'the doll's house: 3', 'the grand's legs: c', 'making is good, but not too many useless things: only what is needed and useful and fun, concisely').** The doll's house: the corner stones in a pastel per floor, the floor's wallpaper colour (TH_Q_TINT), nothing else coloured, paper plain; the ?house= setting goes. The grand (PB_INST): legs 16 longer, the lyre and pedals down with them, the lid on a shorter stick (0.72), scaled into its old 210 x 120 box. One activity per idea: out of their steps (they stay in the toolbox) My word tune (Spell it on the keys does it), Loud and soft your way (From pp to f), Drive the tempo (Four tempo words), Make a rhythm card (the step has its own card), Climb the ladders (The five Cs), My tune my chords (Chords for a melody). The Piano's Story's play goes inside the pads it repeated: Pluck, push or strike is played on a keyboard (near the front strong, near the back gentle) with the bass that goes round; The pedals' free part is the playground (its quiz stays); Grand, upright, 88 keys has the slide instead of two key rows and four buttons; Strum the strings stays. The in-a-row game (DY: a pill under every asking activity, five in a row a star) was built and set aside: a layer on a hundred activities is not concise. Test sc/dx804.js. |",
]
